From 200b5760cea3b03a156e670dd424bf653def1140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:59:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-19: WPF Order -- Bring to Front / Forward / Send
 Backward / to Back (0.19.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a web page the element later in the source is drawn on top, so Order is
the element's place among its siblings in the source -- like the WPF designer
reordering the XAML; the page is drawn again and the component tree follows.
- Right-click > 順序: 移到最上層 / 上移一層 / 下移一層 / 移到最下層, with the
  Blend keys Ctrl+Shift+] / Ctrl+] / Ctrl+[ / Ctrl+Shift+[.
- A fieldset's <legend> and a panel's caption <span class="pnlCap"> stay first.
- Already on top / at the bottom: a status note, nothing changed.
- One WorkspaceEdit (one Ctrl+Z); an element alone on its line moves as that
  line, so front then back leaves the source byte-identical.
- lib/htmlblock.js: parentOf (one pass with a stack), childrenOf, reorder.

Tests: lib 114 (back after the legend / front / forward / backward / already
there; line moves; HotPlate Panel2 with its caption span), smoke 75, real VS
Code 78 (front: the re-drawn tree lists spbSave after sbtExit; one undo puts
it back), probe, panels -- all pass; opened files MD5-unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
